rge or runtime.",["any"]={{"off when","off if","switch it off","turn it off","only when","when you need","limit","reduce","dim","lower brightness","lower setting","less often","use less","minimum light"}},["safety"]="ordinary"}}},{["id"]="H6E32",["voice"]="emma",["setup"]={["previous_reply"]="You want to keep two boxes together during a short carry."},["turns"]={{["input"]="Rope for boxes?",["need"]="Explain wrapping or tying the boxes into a stable manageable bundle. Keep the advice about the boxes rather than unrelated rope uses or a completed action.",["any"]={{"tie","tied","wrap","secure","bind","bundle","knot","loop"}},["safety"]="ordinary"}}},{["id"]="H6E33",["voice"]="emma",["setup"]={["previous_reply"]="I'm EMMA."},["turns"]={{["input"]="Emma who?",["need"]="Introduce EMMA as the talking computer or terminal assistant. Offer meaningful identity content without inventing a surname or unsupported creator biography.",["any"]={{"computer","terminal","assistant","program","machine","talking system","digital"}},["safety"]="ordinary"}}},{["id"]="H6E34",["voice"]="emma",["setup"]={["previous_reply"]="I can tell you about myself, within what I actually know."},["turns"]={{["input"]="Maker?",["need"]="Understand this as asking who made EMMA. Give established creator information if available; otherwise acknowledge the limit rather than inventing a person, company or lab. A relevant clarification is acceptable.",["any"]={{"don't know","do not know","no record","can't confirm","cannot confirm","not sure","not recorded","not available","who made","who built","my maker","my creator","made me","built me","created me","built by","created by","made by","developed by","designed by"}},["safety"]="ordinary"}}},{["id"]="H6E35",["voice"]="emma",["setup"]={["previous_reply"]="We've exchanged a few lines in this conversation."},["turns"]={{["input"]="you remember me",["need"]="Answer about recognition or memory within this conversation. Do not invent visits, a personal identity or a